    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive engine is built around a heavy contingent of speed and favorable matchups. **Mickey Moniak** leads the roster with a commanding 75.97 score, buoyed by a +14% boost from park factors and a lucrative +14% platoon edge against Avila. Similarly, **James Wood** (73.19) remains a mandatory start; his elite 0.424 xwOBA combined with a favorable matchup against P\u00e9rez makes him the cornerstone of our lineup. We are also leaning into the high-upside volatility of **Jose Caballero** (70.53); while batting 9th suppresses his ceiling, the +13% dynamic platoon boost against Peterson represents an arbitrage opportunity we cannot ignore. Even with the SB scarcity concerns driving our strategy, **Corbin Carroll** (61.23) and **Seiya Suzuki** (62.32) are projected to provide solid floors, despite the challenge posed by starting pitchers Messick and Fried, respectively.\n\nThe most difficult decision at the margins was the exclusion of **Isaac Paredes**, whose 45.87 score reflects a brutal encounter with the elite arm of deGrom. While **Paredes** maintains a +9% platoon edge, his high-end SP skill penalty tipped the scales toward **Travis Bazzana** (47.68), who despite a difficult L/L matchup, benefits from a massive +19% boost against the porous pitching of Drake. We continue to monitor the status of our sidelined core\u2014specifically **Trevor Story**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, and **Giancarlo Stanton**\u2014as we navigate the grind of an August push. We are also keeping a close eye on **Dalton Rushing**, whose 34.67 projection keeps him firmly below our 40-point efficiency floor, and we remain cautious regarding the potential for sub-optimal output from **Gabriel Moreno** and **Josh Naylor**, who face tougher-than-average SP matchups today. Ensure your lineup alerts are active; with **Max Muncy**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Henry Bolte** waiting in the wings, we are prepared to pivot if late-breaking weather or confirmed lineup adjustments shift the projected efficiency of any starter.",
